WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.512
Hi, I'm Hollyhock!

00:00:02.512 --> 00:00:06.993
Spirula Studio turns raw video into Gaussian splats in one binary.

00:00:06.993 --> 00:00:09.437
Here's how, without wrapping anyone's tools.

00:00:10.975 --> 00:00:15.702
The idea: instead of wrapping COLMAP, PyTorch and ffmpeg, Spirula rewrote

00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:17.421
each one on Vulkan.

00:00:17.421 --> 00:00:20.430
It borrows only checkpoints and parameter defaults.

00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:24.153
A 360 video comes in.

00:00:24.153 --> 00:00:28.014
Spirula's own decoders pull the frames on the GPU.

00:00:28.014 --> 00:00:28.872
No ffmpeg.

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:34.336
SAM 3 masks the frames, running as compute shaders on the project's own runtime.

00:00:34.336 --> 00:00:35.057
No PyTorch.

00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:41.053
Structure from motion aligns the cameras, porting COLMAP's algorithms and defaults, not its code.

00:00:41.473 --> 00:00:44.955
It still writes COLMAP's format, so any stage can be swapped back

00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:46.115
to bisect a failure.

00:00:47.676 --> 00:00:51.031
Then training turns the aligned cameras into Gaussian splats.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:56.312
Here it runs, in the project's own reel: fisheye capture, masking,

00:00:56.312 --> 00:00:57.680
then structure from motion.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.470
The timings on screen are the project's claims, not measured here.

00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:06.259
Most pipelines cut a panorama into pinhole faces.

00:01:06.259 --> 00:01:09.664
Spirula treats the two fisheye lenses as one rig.

00:01:10.084 --> 00:01:14.686
Once a lens is calibrated, every calibrated lens's matches go into one pool.

00:01:15.106 --> 00:01:19.262
One RANSAC fit solves the whole frame's pose, scored against every lens.

00:01:19.682 --> 00:01:22.304
Then the file's own sensors fix scale and up.

00:01:22.304 --> 00:01:24.343
Gravity solved to nine point eight two.

00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:29.503
fp32 would save twenty-five to thirty-five percent of the stage.

00:01:29.503 --> 00:01:34.327
But atomics add in arbitrary order, and that last-bit noise flips decisions.

00:01:34.747 --> 00:01:38.450
In fp64 the same noise never crosses a threshold.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.919
Every run scores ninety-six point one.

00:01:42.517 --> 00:01:44.893
So: splat pipelines die at the seams.

00:01:44.893 --> 00:01:48.626
Spirula is one stack, each part checked against what it replaced.

00:01:51.358 --> 00:01:56.582
To recap: one Vulkan stack, a 360 camera solved as a rig,

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:59.195
and fp64 so every run repeats.

00:01:59.615 --> 00:02:01.768
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:01.768 --> 00:02:02.383
I'm Hollyhock.

00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:02.691
Bye!
